## Graphical Abstract
Heteroatoms $(Z\mathrm{n}{+}\mathrm{C})$ and cyano (- $\therefore C\equiv\mathrm{N}$ group co-decorated porous $\mathrm{g-C}_{3}\mathrm{N}_{4}$ nanosheets were synthesized, exhibiting enhanced photocatalytic $\mathrm{H}_{2}$ evolution and U(VI) reduction activity.
## Highlights
Heteroatoms and cyano ( $\mathbf{\partial}_{-C}\equiv\mathbf{N}_{,}$ ) group co-decorated $\mathrm{g-C}_{3}\mathrm{N}_{4}$ nanosheets is synthesized.   
Heteroatoms $(Z\mathrm{n}{+}\mathrm{C})$ doping modulates band gap and prolongs electron lifetime. Cyano group broadens light response range and acts as electron-withdrawing group. Massive nanopores in nanosheets provide more reaction sites and diffusion channels.   
The optimized photocatalyst displays a maximum $\mathrm{H}_{2}$ evolution rate of \~484.09 μmol/h.
